From: Yaron Shahrabani <yarons@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: Exposure compensation for the software ISP and its Android HAL support

Soft IPA: the Agc algorithm registers ExposureValue (-2.0 to 2.0) and moves
the target of its regulation by it. The mean sample value it regulates is
not proportional to the exposure, so a unit is not an exact photographic
stop; the value is reported back in the metadata.

Android HAL: cameras with controls::ExposureValue report a compensation
range in steps of 1/2 EV instead of [0, 0], AE_EXPOSURE_COMPENSATION is
translated to ExposureValue and echoed in the results. The brightness slider
of camera applications did nothing before.
---
--- a/src/android/camera_capabilities.cpp
+++ b/src/android/camera_capabilities.cpp
@@ -997,15 +997,24 @@
 	staticMetadata_->addEntry(ANDROID_CONTROL_AE_AVAILABLE_MODES,
 				  aeAvailableModes);
 
+	/* Exposure compensation in steps of 1/2 EV, for cameras that have it. */
 	std::vector<int32_t> aeCompensationRange = {
 		0, 0,
 	};
+	camera_metadata_rational_t aeCompensationStep[] = {
+		{ 0, 1 }
+	};
+	const auto exposureValueInfo = camera_->controls().find(&controls::ExposureValue);
+	if (exposureValueInfo != camera_->controls().end()) {
+		aeCompensationRange = {
+			static_cast<int32_t>(exposureValueInfo->second.min().get<float>() * 2),
+			static_cast<int32_t>(exposureValueInfo->second.max().get<float>() * 2),
+		};
+		aeCompensationStep[0] = { 1, 2 };
+	}
 	staticMetadata_->addEntry(ANDROID_CONTROL_AE_COMPENSATION_RANGE,
 				  aeCompensationRange);
 
-	const camera_metadata_rational_t aeCompensationStep[] = {
-		{ 0, 1 }
-	};
 	staticMetadata_->addEntry(ANDROID_CONTROL_AE_COMPENSATION_STEP,
 				  aeCompensationStep);
 
